ommit_sha":"2a6333719b1dec732cc4e3620fca2c00e9f07b1d","position":"1788909390186423001-1da14dcf-be29-47d4-8769-103eaf7c65be"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation committed at 6780420d70b991238b103663cff1a83ba98e0d20. Comments and docstrings changed only across the 12 allowlisted blocks in three tests/external files. Historical, repeated, emphatic, and ornamental prose was removed while preserving the provider matrix, raw artifacts, deterministic helper ownership, Jira shape contract, workflow routing, terminal-stage contract, and plan-variable guard. Evidence includes PASS results for normalized non-docstring AST and exact directives, the reviewed-block allowlist guard, comment hygiene, scoped Ruff and format checks, seven-test external collection, 15 hermetic consumer tests, pre-commit repository lint and typecheck, diff integrity, and commit-ticket validation. Per operator direction, full make verify is deferred to Gerrit CI. The leaf awaits its independent 12-row receipt and Gerrit availability. It has not been pushed or closed.","timestamp":1788828255235669001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CHANGES REQUIRED on a4d17373b49e1ed3958fe92d03397dfc853c3283: independent accuracy review found four documentation defects. The structured-output module said only provider calls occur there although deterministic scoring/artifact work also occurs; only those calls are live. It also attributed default exclusion to both external and llm_live, although external excludes while llm_live routes provider-matrix selection, and it omitted the distinction between an arm-level credential skip and uncredentialed cells recorded as unmeasured. The verified-fake module referred to one test although it defines four. The workflow module implied both tests traverse review_skeleton although the second invokes live plan review. Corrections are limited to those docstrings; a fresh exact-SHA independent receipt is required.","timestamp":1788901862350707001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Correction milestone: amended the four independently identified documentation inaccuracies into exact SHA 5910522937af8e35994d9b9efeb50de5c1a5a6fe while preserving Change-Id I67d22f30f5c0b1e330cbe9ea79732d5efd6e6640. Verification on that SHA: normalized non-docstring AST/directive guard PASS; seven external tests collect; 15 focused hermetic consumer tests pass; path-scoped diff check PASS; repository pre-commit lint and typecheck PASS; commit-ticket trailer PASS; worktree clean. Per operator direction, full make verify remains delegated to Gerrit CI. This corrected SHA now requires a fresh independent 12-row semantic/bloat receipt before push/closure.","timestamp":1788902070665587001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CHANGES REQUIRED on 5910522937af8e35994d9b9efeb50de5c1a5a6fe. The independent 12-block review found three semicolons prohibited by the documentation policy, two uses of live as a value adjective, and a broken 1 and 3 comment sequence. No receipt was posted. Semantic preservation, bloat reduction, normalized runtime AST, directives, scope, hygiene, Ruff, formatting, seven-test collection, 15 focused tests, diff integrity, trailer validation, and clean worktree all passed.","timestamp":1788909021765244001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Policy corrections amended at exact SHA 1f0a8088932e6164925097421f31270d5985b3bc. Change-Id I67d22f30f5c0b1e330cbe9ea79732d5efd6e6640. Provider-backed behavior is now described by mechanism, the prohibited semicolons are removed, and the workflow comments retain the 1, 2, 3 sequence. The prose-only guard, seven-test collection, 15 focused consumer tests, diff integrity, trailer validation, repository lint and typecheck, and clean worktree all pass. Full make verify is deferred to Gerrit CI per operator direction. A fresh independent 12-row receipt is still required.","timestamp":1788909390186423001}],"created_at":1788570998536316864,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"04a7e5bc-2be6-4f52-b573-dc50c9204005","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"5be5-06e4-cf6b-4a6b"},{"link_uuid":"cc870e6e-3a38-45d4-880a-574fb2111e13","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"8839-6895-7904-425e"},{"link_uuid":"f8cfa027-6fa3-4a39-986b-fd6cb81c0683","relation":"supersedes","target_id":"0142-bb14-7a55-47aa"},{"link_uuid":"b0a4a505-0630-49a3-9ae0-e48a7357a2bd","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e5b4-b1a9-a2d9-4909"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThree external-test modules contain repeated, historical, decorative, or obvious prose. Their contents are unchanged from the audit and revalidated on `origin/main` at `0033662b5534531d84e39d4a14bf75c8e768e85e`.\n\n## Approach\nCondense only the listed blocks. Preserve non-docstring AST, runtime fixture data, sentinels, markers, assertions, and exact directives. Keep live-test intent complete without duplicating assertions or helper-owned logic.\n\n## Scope\n- `test_structured_output_matrix.py:1-22,49-53,114-120,139-144,193` — Preserve live-call-only scope; exact provider × directive × production-prompt × repeat matrix; raw artifacts; helper ownership of deterministic scoring/credentials/budgets; the agentic first-object trap plus single-shot control; one unparsed text-mode call; and partial-run/all-skip semantics. Delete the obvious score-table narration at 193.\n- `test_verified_fake_contract_live.py:1-18` — Preserve shared-contract/real-client purpose, fixture-recapture drift signal, opt-in requirements, and separate authenticated-`acli` requirement for search.\n- `test_workflow_live.py:1-15,37-39,69,91-98,110-111,115` — Preserve real `RunnerAgentStep`, `review_skeleton` stage path, live prompt resolution, provider routing, terminal-step contract, and the guarantee that missing `{{plan}}` in verify/coach does not degrade to `INDETERMINATE`; delete comments already made obvious by assertions/docstrings.\n\nRetain out-of-scope sentinel, production-spacing, budget, provider-selection, stable-key, non-vacuity, replay, security-overlay, schema, and fixture-data comments. Consumers include structured-output and external-integration workflows, external conftest gates/fixtures, shared Jira-shape contracts, hermetic counterparts, documented live checks, provider/scorer tests, and live-reachability guards. No autodoc/`__doc__` consumer exists. Preserve the `import rebar  # noqa: F401` directive exactly.\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The leaf commit changes only comments/true docstrings or blank lines in the declared, reviewed blocks; non-docstring AST, runtime strings, assertions, and exact directives remain unchanged.\n- [ ] A reviewer who did not author the remediation posts a leaf-linked TSV with one row per edited block: path/block, pinned before citation, final-commit after citation (or DELETED plus neighbor), preserved contract/consumer, before/after words, semantic-preservation verdict, bloat-removal verdict, and reviewer session.\n- [ ] Every row has `semantic-preservation=PASS` and `bloat-removal=PASS`; bloat removal requires shorter text with repetition/history/ornament removed rather than relocated.\n- [ ] Recorded focused checks, path-scoped `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv `make verify` pass.\n- [ ] Missing or FAIL rows block closure.\n\n## Verification\nRun the recorded normalized AST/directive guard, focused tests, diff check, and `make verify`. The independent TSV judges prose quality.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/external/test_structured_output_matrix.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/external/test_verified_fake_contract_live.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."},{"path":"tests/external/test_workflow_live.py","reason":"Condense comments/docstrings while preserving the scoped contract."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","2d43-3c39-307e-4450"],["relates_to","e5b4-b1a9-a2d9-4909"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2d43-3c39-307e-4450","parent_status_uuid":"97306218-358f-493e-b12e-26a25c690af0","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_id":"3187-eae2-a522-43cd","ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in tests/external — cohort 02: structured_output_matrix–workflow_live","verify_commands":[{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -c 'import ast, io, re, subprocess, sys, tokenize\nOWNERS = (ast.Module, ast.ClassDef, ast.FunctionDef, ast.AsyncFunctionDef)\nPAT = re.compile(r\"#\\s*(?:noqa\\b|type:\\s*ignore\\b|pragma:\\s*no cover\\b|pyright:|mypy:|ruff:|pylint:|(?:fmt|isort):\\s*(?:on|off|skip)\\b|nosec\\b|coding[:=]|[A-Za-z][\\w-]*-ok:)\", re.I)\nclass Strip(ast.NodeTransformer):\n    def generic_visit(self, node):\n        node = super().generic_visit(node)\n        if isinstance(node, OWNERS) and node.body and isinstance(node.body[0], ast.Expr) and isinstance(node.body[0].value, ast.Constant) and isinstance(node.body[0].value.value, str):\n            node.body.pop(0)\n        return node\ndef src(ref, path):\n    return subprocess.check_output([\"git\", \"show\", f\"{ref}:{path}\"], text=True)\ndef norm(text, path):\n    tree = Strip().visit(ast.parse(text, filename=path, type_comments=True))\n    for node in ast.walk(tree):\n        if isinstance(node, ast.TypeIgnore): node.lineno = 0\n    return ast.dump(tree, annotate_fields=True, include_attributes=False)\ndef directives(text):\n    lines = text.splitlines()\n    selected = [lines[tok.start[0]-1] for tok in tokenize.generate_tokens(io.StringIO(text).readline) if tok.type == tokenize.COMMENT and PAT.search(tok.string)]\n    return (lines[0] if lines and lines[0].startswith(\"#!\") else \"\"), selected\nbad_ast, bad_directives = [], []\nfor path in sys.argv[1:]:\n    before, after = src(\"HEAD^\", path), src(\"HEAD\", path)\n    if norm(before, path) != norm(after, path): bad_ast.append(path)\n    if directives(before) != directives(after): bad_directives.append(path)\nassert not bad_ast, f\"non-docstring AST changes: {bad_ast}\"\nassert not bad_directives, f\"directive/shebang changes: {bad_directives}\"' tests/external/test_structured_output_matrix.py tests/external/test_verified_fake_contract_live.py tests/external/test_workflow_live.py","dd_id":"python-prose-only","dd_text":"Require normalized non-docstring AST equality and exact directive/shebang lines."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest --collect-only -q tests/external/test_structured_output_matrix.py tests/external/test_verified_fake_contract_live.py tests/external/test_workflow_live.py","dd_id":"external-collection","dd_text":"Prove all three external modules still collect through their real markers and fixtures."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest -q tests/unit/test_structured_matrix_scorer.py tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/jira_contract/test_verified_fake_contract.py tests/unit/test_ci_provider_matrix.py::test_every_module_using_the_shared_live_gate_declares_the_marker_sentinel tests/unit/test_external_canary.py::test_modifyitems_marks_jira_gated_module tests/unit/test_external_tier_live_reachability.py::test_external_plan_review_fixture_clears_the_blocking_det_floor","dd_id":"external-consumer-contracts","dd_text":"Exercise scorer, verified-fake, sentinel, Jira gate, and live-reachability contracts hermetically."},{"command":"rtk git diff --check HEAD^ HEAD -- tests/external/test_structured_output_matrix.py tests/external/test_verified_fake_contract_live.py tests/external/test_workflow_live.py","dd_id":"diff-integrity","dd_text":"Reject whitespace errors in all declared paths."},{"command":"rtk env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify","dd_id":"repository-gates","dd_text":"Run complete repository verification before review."}]},"source_event_uuids":["54f8b135-fff7-4125-a480-5f902c105726","9e57e42e-c622-4f7d-b777-45e90773728a","034e442c-25c7-4076-976d-8d5853de1149","97306218-358f-493e-b12e-26a25c690af0","af5906e3-e767-4b00-afe2-06c19d94a899","3defd28f-63e3-44cb-ae57-12792f40208a","b0a4a505-0630-49a3-9ae0-e48a7357a2bd","5a233632-29cd-4ac4-94ae-5a6f3a690e43","0fc3ac34-da98-44d3-9a53-f8b37337def1","c5026b86-2946-433f-8a5b-d76b8d3e6aa0","1da14dcf-be29-47d4-8769-103eaf7c65be"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788909390186423002,"uuid":"9f530bfa-6a33-4c8a-a2d5-f5a09b738e10"}